</code>

This assertion is based on a comment that says "@@@ ArrayList count increases by 1 when an item is added". The Count of the ArrayList increases when an item is added to it, so we are asserting that the old count plus one (which is the operation of adding an item) will always be less than or equal to the current count of the ArrayList.
--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) + 1 = RET);
</code>

Here, `OLD(_size)` refers to the value of `_size` at the beginning of the function, `+ 1` adds 1 to the old value of `_size` to account for the addition of a new element, and `RET` refers to the return value of the function, which is the current value of `_size` after the addition. The `OLD(x)` and `RET` syntax are used to ensure the assertion is based on the start state of the function and its end state.
